\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Membership and substructure, showing the two operations separately. \emph  {Left:} sky distribution of the 1,392{} members with $P > 0.5$, coloured and directly labelled by kinematic subgroup, with lower-probability candidates in grey and the manual quality-exempt spectroscopic anchors marked by open squares. Association membership used $(l, b, \varpi , \mu _{\alpha *}, \mu _\delta )$, \emph  {including} parallax. \emph  {Right:} the proper-motion plane. The subgroup labels themselves come from $(l, b, \mu _{\alpha *}, \mu _\delta )$ only, with parallax excluded at this stage and not at the previous one.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
