\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The age evidence. \emph  {Top:} extinction-corrected colour--magnitude diagrams for the three subgroups on the baseline branch, with the other subgroups' members in grey, spectroscopic anchors as open squares, and both isochrone families drawn at the adopted counts-based age of that subgroup. The observational scatter within a panel and the PARSEC-versus-MIST separation between the curves are different quantities and are drawn differently. \emph  {Bottom left:} the counts-based age of every fit cell, by subgroup and family, with the baseline branch marked and the retained upper-main-sequence envelope (2.00--4.01\,Myr) shaded; Cyg~OB2-B's cells pile up against the top of its own prior grid. \emph  {Bottom right:} what that envelope costs in supernovae.}}{8}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
