\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces The $^{60}$Fe forecast against COSI's expected sensitivity, for every headline branch, on each of the three published yield arms fixed before any flux was computed. The separation between arms is far larger than the spread across the whole census branch set, which is why a measurement constrains the IMF and the yield model jointly rather than the IMF alone. On the recommended arm of \citet  {limongi2018} every progenitor collapses directly and the predicted flux is identically zero.}}{15}{figure.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:isotopes}{{11}{15}{The $^{60}$Fe forecast against COSI's expected sensitivity, for every headline branch, on each of the three published yield arms fixed before any flux was computed. The separation between arms is far larger than the spread across the whole census branch set, which is why a measurement constrains the IMF and the yield model jointly rather than the IMF alone. On the recommended arm of \citet {limongi2018} every progenitor collapses directly and the predicted flux is identically zero}{figure.11}{}}
