\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.1}{\ignorespaces The three kinematic subgroups on the baseline branch (PARSEC, $R_V = 3.1$, $\alpha = 2.3$, $\delta = 0$). The age is the counts-based age the ledger consumes, not the colour--magnitude prior. Closure is the grid median over the six family--$R_V$ cells at $\alpha = 2.3$, and the closing slope is the slope at which that subgroup's census would close exactly. A $\times $ in the fit-status column marks a subgroup whose baseline mass-function fit failed the residual-fit criterion; none does.}}{17}{table.A.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:subgroups}{{A.1}{17}{The three kinematic subgroups on the baseline branch (PARSEC, $R_V = 3.1$, $\alpha = 2.3$, $\delta = 0$). The age is the counts-based age the ledger consumes, not the colour--magnitude prior. Closure is the grid median over the six family--$R_V$ cells at $\alpha = 2.3$, and the closing slope is the slope at which that subgroup's census would close exactly. A $\times $ in the fit-status column marks a subgroup whose baseline mass-function fit failed the residual-fit criterion; none does}{table.A.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.2}{\ignorespaces Validation status for each scientific analysis stage and the consequence carried downstream. \textsc  {partial} means the stage was usable while a named criterion or limitation remained; the failure is reported in the text and was not reinterpreted.}}{17}{table.A.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:validation}{{A.2}{17}{Validation status for each scientific analysis stage and the consequence carried downstream. \textsc {partial} means the stage was usable while a named criterion or limitation remained; the failure is reported in the text and was not reinterpreted}{table.A.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.3}{\ignorespaces The three factors of the conditional scenario-availability score $S = C_1 C_3 C_4$, with what each one actually is. Only $C_1$ is a sampled probability. The product is therefore a scenario score, not a calibrated probability, and the paper does not present it as one.}}{17}{table.A.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cocoon}{{A.3}{17}{The three factors of the conditional scenario-availability score $S = C_1 C_3 C_4$, with what each one actually is. Only $C_1$ is a sampled probability. The product is therefore a scenario score, not a calibrated probability, and the paper does not present it as one}{table.A.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {A.4}{\ignorespaces The 54\ all-explode branches, their mass-function fit-quality status and their results. Family PA = PARSEC, MI = MIST. $\delta $ is the star-formation duration in Myr. Columns A, B, C give the residual-fit verdict for each subgroup at that family, $R_V$ and $\alpha $; \emph  {all} is their conjunction. $\Sigma $ is the star-weighted association closure ratio. $S$ is the conditional scenario-availability score of Sect.~\ref  {sec:cocoon}, \emph  {not} a calibrated probability. Branches with $\alpha = 2.6$ are sensitivity cases outside the headline set. The complete table, including per-subgroup closure ratios, black-hole-threshold columns and Poisson intervals, is available electronically.}}{18}{table.A.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:branches}{{A.4}{18}{The \NSNallbranches \ all-explode branches, their mass-function fit-quality status and their results. Family PA = PARSEC, MI = MIST. $\delta $ is the star-formation duration in Myr. Columns A, B, C give the residual-fit verdict for each subgroup at that family, $R_V$ and $\alpha $; \emph {all} is their conjunction. $\Sigma $ is the star-weighted association closure ratio. $S$ is the conditional scenario-availability score of Sect.~\ref {sec:cocoon}, \emph {not} a calibrated probability. Branches with $\alpha = 2.6$ are sensitivity cases outside the headline set. The complete table, including per-subgroup closure ratios, black-hole-threshold columns and Poisson intervals, is available electronically}{table.A.4}{}}
